// PLAYTEST: does a 15-point boost to every decompile attempt change how you
// fight, or only how the odds line reads?
//
// The seventh of seven class files — see `player-class-striker.ron` for the
// shared argument: why the pack is this pack, why the pool is unspent, and
// why the headless bin reports the same numbers for every class.
//
//     FERAL_DEV_ARENA=1 cargo run  ->  [R] Arena  ->  [L] player-class-decompiler
//
// **The bin is blinder here than for any other class.** It plays
// `PartyPlan::AllAttack`, which never spends a turn on a decompile at all,
// so the headless numbers are not merely a floor without the class — they
// are a floor without the verb. Everything this class is worth happens in
// the real UI.
//
// The pack matters differently for this one. Five sub_processes a group is
// a lot of bodies to try attempts on, which is what you want, but they are
// also cheap: if the class only reads on programs you would not have kept
// anyway, that is the finding.
//
// What to watch:
//   - The odds line, first. `Game::player_decompiler_bonuses` feeds the two
//     screens that *show* odds and the one that *rolls* them, so a class
//     term that reached the roll but not the display would show here as a
//     number that lands better than it reads.
//   - Whether the boost changes the decision. It multiplies the whole
//     attempt rather than softening the target's Integrity term, so it is
//     worth the same on a full-health program as on a beaten one. Does that
//     make it worth trying *early*, before spending rounds weakening
//     something? That is the behaviour the class is supposed to buy, and it
//     is the one to falsify.
//   - Whether 15 points is felt at all against a species' own resistance.
//     It is an argued number, not a measured one — `balance_sim` models no
//     decompiling, so this fight is the only instrument there is.
//   - The Decompiler raises no affinity, so `bit_rot_v2` runs at neutral
//     and the damped Damage axis never shows in this kit. The class must
//     justify itself on attempts alone.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 5, zone: 1),
    character: (
        class: Some(Decompiler),
        stats: (0, 0, 0, 0),
        routine: Some("bit_rot_v2"),
    ),
    party: [
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
    ],
    opponents: [
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
    ],
    reps: 1,
    seed: 2,
)
